# XSH thrd_create()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# thrd_nomem / thrd_error (resource limits) cannot be forced portably and
# are not tested. The locale case needs an installed second locale and is
# left out. A thread's ID is compared only while the thread is alive.

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.001
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_create() returns thrd_success; the new thread calls func
           exactly once, with arg; data the creator wrote before the call is
           seen by the new thread; thrd_join() returns thrd_success with
           func's return value.
test       t/001-runs-func.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.002
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       The identifier stored by thrd_create() equals (thrd_equal()) what
           thrd_current() returns in the new thread; two threads alive at the
           same time have different identifiers, and neither equals the
           creator's.
test       t/002-stores-id.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.003
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       When func returns, the thread ends as if thrd_exit() had been
           called with that value: thrd_join() obtains the value (a negative
           one too), and the destructor of a thread-specific key the thread
           had set is called once with the value.
test       t/003-return-is-exit.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.004
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread created while SIGUSR1 is blocked and SIGUSR2 is unblocked
           in the creator starts with SIGUSR1 blocked and SIGUSR2 unblocked.
test       t/004-sigmask.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.005
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A signal pending for the creator (blocked SIGUSR1, sent to it with
           pthread_kill()) is not pending in the new thread.
test       t/005-pending-empty.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.006
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       With an alternate signal stack set in the creator, the new thread
           has none (sigaltstack() reports it disabled).
test       t/006-altstack.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_create.007
anchor     functions/thrd_create.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A thread created after the creator's rounding direction was
           changed starts with that rounding direction.
note       NOTINUSE when no direction other than the current one can be set.
test       t/007-fenv.c
